"""layers.0.mlp.down_proj:5138 — a "di" spelling detector.

The component reads the current token and writes a negative value when that
token spells the syllable "di" (or "dis", "dig", "dit", "div", "dy", ...), with
the strength falling as the fragment gets longer and more word-like. It is
strongest on a bare "di" (Italian "di", "Di" names, the katakana/Cyrillic/Chinese
"di" syllables), weaker on "di"-prefixes, and near zero elsewhere.

Tokens are normalised to their lowercase letters, so " di", "-di", ".Di" and "DI"
all count as "di". Predictions are the rough activation levels for each class.
