Singular 'word'/'Word' is strongest. Plurals, strings containing 'word',
translations, spelling vocabulary, and related computing names are weaker.
Case, leading whitespace, and code punctuation modulate the singular response.
The idiom 'other words' is weaker. Selected suffixes, prepositions, and
quotation marks immediately after 'word' retain a response. Everything else
is zero. Previous-token state resets between documents.
